Scott defines the Smyth power domain by \(\mathbb{P}\mathcal{D}=\{\bigcup_{i<n}(\downarrow X_i)\mid \forall i<n.\, X_i\in\mathcal{D}\}\), with \(\downarrow X=\{Y\in\mathcal{D}\mid Y\subseteq X\}\) and with the empty union admitted when \(n=0\); he prepares \(\mathcal{D}\) by the isomorphic system \(\mathcal{D}^\dagger=\{\downarrow X\mid X\in\mathcal{D}\}\) so that the construct is the finite-union closure of that preparation, and he records that \(\downarrow X\cap\downarrow Y\neq\emptyset\) if and only if \(\{X,Y\}\) is consistent, in which case the intersection equals \(\downarrow(X\cap Y)\). `PDmem` is that family: a set `W` of neighbourhoods lies in it when `W` equals the union of `upSet X` over a finite list of neighbourhoods, and `upSet X` is `{Y | V.mem Y ∧ Y ⊆ X}`, which is the displayed down-set. The empty list is the empty union, and `PDmem_empty` proves \(\emptyset\) is a neighbourhood by extensionality against `mem_PDunion`. `PDmem_upSet` realises a single down-set by a singleton list, `PDmem_master` specialises that to the master, and `PDmem_iff_fin` rewrites the list as Scott’s indexed union over `Fin n`. `PDmem_union` closes the family under binary union by concatenating the witnessing lists. `dagger` is `powerSystem`, the preparation whose neighbourhoods are these down-sets, and `dagger_isomorphic` is `isomorphic_powerSystem`. `upSet_inter_nonempty_iff` rewrites the intersection of down-sets as the down-set of the intersection and identifies nonempty membership with a neighbourhood \(Z\subseteq X\cap Y\). `dagger_upSet_inter` uses that witness, the intersection law, and the same rewrite to place \(\downarrow X\cap\downarrow Y\) among the neighbourhoods of \(\mathcal{D}^\dagger\). **Theorem:** yes — `PDmem` is the set of finite unions of down-sets, including the empty union, and `dagger` is the preparation \(\mathcal{D}^\dagger\). **Proof:** yes — the isomorphism is the power-system isomorphism, the meeting of down-sets is the consistency witness \(Z\subseteq X\cap Y\), and the empty union, principal down-sets, and binary union are `PDmem_empty`, `PDmem_upSet`, and `PDmem_union`.
